{"Contradiction between test showing fallback to DB on outdated cache as implicit invalidation and assertion that there is no invalidation path for denial cache entries after permission grant - needs investigation": 0.1449316143989563, "newRemoteRBACClient constructs a gRPC client using insecure credentials by default if clientCfg.certFile is empty, making communications with the remote AuthZ service susceptible to MITM or eavesdropping": 0.09968449920415878, "ProvideAuthZClient wires a NoopCache for in-proc authz clients, preventing client-side caching, and no unit tests verify the NoopCache contract or confirm the in-proc path uses NoopCache as intended": 0.20155081152915955, "No tests exercise concurrent access to the authz caches and service paths, risking data races or race conditions under concurrent load with the local in-memory caches protected by singleflight": 0.06554155051708221, "New denial cache key function userPermDenialCacheKey introduced to support per-resource denial caching, distinguishing denial entries from allow entries": 0.05339482054114342}